    {
      "recommendationid": "224615818",
      "author": {
        "steamid": "76561199025735503",
        "personaname": "BarLak",
        "persona_status": "offline",
        "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199025735503/",
        "num_games_owned": 0,
        "num_reviews": 12,
        "playtime_forever": 692,
        "playtime_last_two_weeks": 692,
        "playtime_at_review": 301,
        "last_played": 1777771361,
        "avatar": "9dab8056e33915b42b6beadff8b7c6b4c817b034"
      },
      "language": "english",
      "review": "No Man’s Sky is one of the most underrated games of our time, and honestly, it deserves way more recognition than it gets. What started as a rocky launch has turned into something truly incredible. The sheer scale of the universe, the freedom to explore, build, trade, and survive—it’s unlike almost anything else out there.\r\n\r\nWhat really blows my mind is the potential this game still has. It already offers hundreds of hours of gameplay, yet it feels like we’ve barely scratched the surface of what it could become. With constant updates and improvements, it’s evolving into something that could genuinely be the “WoW of the future”—a massive, living universe where players can lose themselves for years.\r\n\r\nIf you haven’t tried it yet, you’re missing out on something special. No Man’s Sky isn’t just a game anymore—it’s a growing universe with endless possibilities. Everyone should give it a chance.\r\nOne thing that could take No Man’s Sky to the next level is a deeper player-driven economy. Imagine a real monetary system where players can build actual businesses—gas stations for starships, trading hubs, repair docks, even full-on colonies with services.\r\n\r\nRight now, the game already has the foundation: base building, trading, multiplayer interactions. But if players could truly specialize and earn currency through services, it would transform the universe into something alive—more like a real galactic society.\r\n\r\nIt has the potential to become the “WoW of space,” not just through exploration, but through community and economy. We’re honestly just scratching the surface of what this game could become.",
